    "metric_explanations": {
        "accuracy": "Accuracy measures the overall fraction of correct predictions across all obesity categories. Formula: Correct Predictions / Total Predictions. While intuitive, it can be deceptive if classes are imbalanced.",
        "precision_macro": "Macro Precision measures the average purity of positive predictions across each class independently, giving equal weight to rare and frequent categories. Answering: 'When the model predicts a specific obesity tier, how often is it truly correct?'",
        "precision_weighted": "Weighted Precision calculates the average class precision, weighted by the prevalence of each class in the test set.",
        "recall_macro": "Macro Recall measures the model's ability to detect all individuals belonging to each specific obesity class. Answering: 'Out of all individuals who truly belong to an obesity category, what percentage did the model find?'",
        "recall_weighted": "Weighted Recall computes the sensitivity averaged according to each class's sample support.",
        "f1_macro": "Macro F1-Score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall computed equally across all 7 categories. It serves as the gold-standard validation criterion in multiclass healthcare evaluation because it penalizes poor performance on any single clinical tier.",
        "f1_weighted": "Weighted F1-Score is the prevalence-weighted harmonic mean of precision and recall.",
        "roc_auc_ovr_macro": "Multiclass ROC-AUC (One-vs-Rest) evaluates how effectively the model discriminates each obesity category from the other six classes across all possible probability thresholds. 1.0 represents perfect discrimination."
    },
